        {
          "at": "2026-08-13T17:55:41Z",
          "findings": [
            {
              "category": "inconsistent_decisions",
              "file": "knowledge/adr/2026-08-13-1720-test-obligation-method-anchor-ownership.md",
              "line": 36,
              "message": "D1/D2 leaves a silent verification bypass: when a multi-method entry keeps entry-level `spec_refs` but a method omits optional method-level `spec_refs`, those anchors are not copied to any method obligation, while D2 limits fulfillment evaluation to obligation-owned anchors. The ADR therefore permits a grounded trait-level promise to receive no fulfillment verification without stating how it is resolved.",
              "severity": "P1"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:7d698821ce37f35c389dac14fcfce60d2724b257210bdea2b9971b05c8129bf5",
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain"
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-08-13T18:04:56Z",
          "findings": [
            {
              "category": "inconsistent decisions within the same ADR",
              "file": "knowledge/adr/2026-08-13-1720-test-obligation-method-anchor-ownership.md",
              "line": 40,
              "message": "D1 is internally contradictory: it states that a trait_method obligation owns only the method's `spec_refs` (line 40), but then says single-method traits retain existing behavior (line 42), although the prior ADR defines method-level refs as optional and entry-level refs as the fallback. Clarify whether the method-only ownership rule applies to single-method traits; otherwise the scope of anchor ownership is undecidable.",
              "severity": "P1"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:63dc410521381297f354f1b4a1ba22f1480aa75db64ebb62bcba11a4f032ffa7",
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain"
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-08-13T18:11:27Z",
          "findings": [
            {
              "category": "inconsistent decisions",
              "file": "knowledge/adr/2026-08-13-1720-test-obligation-method-anchor-ownership.md",
              "line": 42,
              "message": "D1 permits a single-method trait to declare a partial `method-level spec_refs` set without requiring coverage or falling back to the entry-level refs. Those omitted entry-level anchors then have no owning obligation, contradicting D2's claim that every entry-level anchor is independently verified and allowing fulfillment to silently bypass them. Require single-method coverage or define fallback for partial declarations.",
              "severity": "P0"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:8bfde04d55db857e50db9f742c6740d5d1ff2cfa59bc926ccf782bee9d20fccc",
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain"
